Title:
SrHollow — LSA Secrets Extraction via Existing VSS Shadow Copy + Inline REGF Parser + AES-256 LSA Decrypt

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
SrHollow is a Windows post-exploitation toolchain to extract and decrypt LSA secrets by reading the SYSTEM and SECURITY registry hives from an existing (or newly created) Volume Shadow Copy. It enumerates `\GLOBAL??` for the newest `HarddiskVolumeShadowCopyN`, optionally creates a restore point via `SRSetRestorePointW`, enables `SeBackupPrivilege`, and reads hive files directly from `\\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\...`. The project includes an inline C# `regf` (registry hive) parser to locate required keys/values without external dependencies. It derives the BootKey (SYSKEY), extracts the LSA AES-256 key from `PolEKList`, and decrypts secrets under `Policy\Secrets`, including `DPAPI_SYSTEM` machine/user keys. It’s primarily useful for Red Teams and pentesters needing credential material/DPAPI capability with a “backup-like” file access profile. Interesting because it avoids live registry APIs and common dumping approaches by leveraging VSS + minimal crypto primitives through `bcrypt.dll`.

Technical Focus:
- VSS shadow copy enumeration/usage via `\GLOBAL??` and `HarddiskVolumeShadowCopyN`
- Privilege enabling (`SeBackupPrivilege`) and raw hive file reads from `GLOBALROOT`
- Offline registry hive parsing (`regf` structures: `nk/vk/lf/lh/li/ri/db/sk`)
- BootKey (SYSKEY) reconstruction from LSA class strings and permutation
- LSA secret decryption (SHA-256 stretching + AES-256-CBC via `bcrypt.dll`)
- DPAPI_SYSTEM extraction (MachineKey/UserKey) for SYSTEM-scoped DPAPI decryption

Use Cases:
- Offline extraction of LSA secrets from a live host using VSS-backed hive reads
- Recovering service account passwords, cached secrets, and other LSA-stored material
- Obtaining `DPAPI_SYSTEM` keys to decrypt SYSTEM DPAPI master keys and protected blobs
- “Low-noise” credential access that resembles legitimate backup agent behavior
- Modular staging in PowerShell for recon → hive collection → decrypt → reporting

Keywords:
LSA secrets, VSS, Volume Shadow Copy, HarddiskVolumeShadowCopy, \GLOBAL??, NtOpenDirectoryObject, NtQueryDirectoryObject, SRSetRestorePointW, SeBackupPrivilege, AdjustTokenPrivileges, CreateFileW, registry hive, REGF, SYSTEM hive, SECURITY hive, BootKey, SYSKEY, PolEKList, AES-256-CBC, SHA-256, bcrypt.dll, DPAPI_SYSTEM, CurrVal, Policy\\Secrets, Windows internals, PowerShell, C#